{{Quote|It's not a knockoff. It's the Ultimatrix. And it's a definite improvement over [[Omnitrix (Original)|the original]]. Wanna see? Not only can I transform into anything you can, but I can also evolve those creatures to their [[Ultimate Forms|Ultimate form]].|[[Albedo]] as [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].<ref name="TFB1">''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]''</ref>}}
The '''Ultimatrix''' was the device that '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ben 10: Ultimate Alien]]''' revolved around. [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] used it to replace the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]], which he destroyed in a [[The Final Battle: Part 2|battle]] with [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]].

The Ultimatrix was removed by [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] in ''[[The Ultimate Enemy: Part 2]]'' after the defeat of [[Dagon]], as well as being replaced by the new, completed [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]].

==Appearance==
The Ultimatrix, despite being called a watch, resembles a vambrace which bore a green gauntlet-like band that extended up to almost halfway up the user's forearm. It is light green in color, with a black rectangular button just below the selection interface, and on the left and right sides lay the wrist couplings which are composed of two small green tubes and beneath the tubes, the circuitry can be seen.

The Ultimatrix's selection interface was identical to the original Omnitrix's dial, with the Galvan tech logo changing color to reflect what mode the Ultimatrix was in.

When [[Albedo]] used it, the Ultimatrix had a red color scheme. After [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] took the Ultimatrix from Albedo, the Ultimatrix became green. This shows that the user can change the color scheme of the Ultimatrix.

In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Heroes United]]'', the Ultimatrix, when drawn in '''[[w:c:generatorrex:Generator Rex|Generator Rex]]''' art style, looked the same except it was dark green in color and the hourglass glowed light green.

