==Modes==
<tabber>
|-|Active=[[File:TP (366).png|thumb|left|Active Mode]]
Active Mode is the Ultimatrix's default mode. Active Mode is active when the Ultimatrix can be used, is fully recharged, and has not detected any problems. It is where the user can select the transformation they want to become; initiate the process of transforming; and stay in said transformation. The actual usage time is 10 minutes at a time.<ref name="MoI"/> However, different factors and actions performed by the user can severely diminish the available usage time: most commonly if the user, while transformed, changes to another form.<ref>[[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen Tennyson]]</ref><ref name="MoI"/> A single chain of 2 transformations limits the combined usage time to no more than 10 minutes, and more often less due to power leakage;{{Refn|[[:File:Dwayne Favorite Alien.PNG]]|group = DM}}{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Transformation Duration.PNG]]|group = DM}} whereas chaining 3 or 4 transformations would leave the user with substantially less combined time than 10 minutes. This is because the action is energy-intensive, and depletes the Ultimatrix's power supply more quickly than staying a single transformations does.{{Refn|[[:File:Original Omnitrix Quick-Change.PNG]]|group = DM}}

|-|Recharge=[[File:HU (992).png|thumb|left|Recharge Mode]]
Like the Omnitrix, Recharge Mode is activated when the Ultimatrix runs out of time. Recharge Mode can stop automatically, once a certain period of time has passed. Recharge Mode's main purpose is to prevent the alien DNA from attaching permanently to its host, but can trigger due to power-heavy operations.<ref name="SS">''[[Simian Says]]''</ref>
[[File:Fame (502.5).png|thumb|Time Out]]
While using the Ultimate Forms, however, Recharge Mode will trigger, as they drain the Ultimatrix's battery too quickly.{{Refn|[[:File:Evolutionary Feature Drained the Ultimatrix's Battery.PNG]]|group = DM|name = battery}}

|-|Collect/Capture=[[File:Fame (304).png|thumb|left|Collect Mode]]
When DNA not present in the [[Codon Stream]] is near the Ultimatrix, it will close its main features until the DNA is scanned.<ref name=FaM>''[[Fame]]''</ref> When a new DNA sample is acquired and added, on occasion, the Ultimatrix can show a visual of almost every alien unlocked, including the new one.<ref name=EFA>''[[Escape From Aggregor]]''</ref>

When scanning DNA that was previously used or already present in the Codon Stream, the Ultimatrix identifies and matches the scanned DNA, then moves the species to an active playlist.<ref name="PN775iM">''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]''</ref>{{Refn|During '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s early run, it was stated that the Ultimatrix could passively scan aliens it already had and move them to active playlists.{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix and Ultimatrix Capture Mode.PNG]]|group = DM}} This is changed in ''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]'', as aliens that the Ultimatrix has DNA sampled in its database can only added to an active playlist when they are directly scanned, as shown when Ben unlocked [[Chamalien]] by scanning [[Prisoner 775]].{{Refn|[[Contradictory Retcons (Classic)|Contradictory Retcons]]|name = retcon|group = BTP}}|group = note}}

[[File:AF (259).png|thumb|The Ultimatrix symbol shooting yellow ray]]
During scanning, the Ultimatrix either pops out and shoots out a yellow ray from the black and yellow part or doesn't pop out but circles and then reveals a hole that shoots out a yellow ray. When in alien form, the Ultimatrix shoots out a yellow ray from the dial.<ref>''[[Andreas' Fault]]''</ref>

The Ultimatrix could scan [[Kevin's Mutations|Kevin's mutations]], but it was programmed not to.{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix and Ultimatrix Could Scan Kevin's Mutations.PNG]]|group = DM|name=kev}}

|-|Reset=[[File:Fused (407).png|thumb|Reset Mode]]
Reset Mode can be activated by Voice Command<ref name="SS"/> or by pressing and holding the Ultimatrix symbol as an alien for two seconds.<ref name="Fused" /> During a resetting period, the Ultimatrix deactivates, charges, and re-activates.<ref name="Fused" /> This can turn off/on some features.<ref name="SS"/> The Ultimatrix can also be Hard Reset using the Voice Command function.<ref name="I13">''[[Inspector 13]]''</ref>

|-|Radiation=[[File:THtH (487).png|thumb|Radiation Mode]]
Radiation Mode is activated when high levels of harmful radiation are detected. The Ultimatrix will beep and flash red. Radiation Mode can be turned off by turning the Ultimatrix symbol to the quarter past position as an alien, or when radiation isn't detected anymore.<ref name="THtH">''[[Too Hot to Handle]]''</ref>

|-|Self-Destruct=[[File:TFB2 (357).png|thumb|left|Self-Destruct]]
When in Self-Destruct Mode, the Ultimatrix counts down until it explodes. Self-Destruct Mode functions as a last resort, should the Ultimatrix fall into the wrong hands. Self-Destruct Mode can be activated and deactivated by Voice Commands, but exclusively recognizes the voice of the user.<ref name="TFB2">''[[The Final Battle: Part 2]]''</ref>
</tabber>

